  note bottom of Blackboard
    **Blackboard** -- Generic shared workspace; instantiated **twice**
    per Run as `SourceBlackboard` and `TargetBlackboard`.

    Both instances are records of THIS class; the difference is
    *which* Panels they host:
    - `SourceBlackboard` -- Pack-declared panels (Pack-namespaced names);
      lifecycle: populated during Source phase, frozen at quiescence
      into a `SourceFreeze` artefact, then quiescent for the rest of
      the Run.
    - `TargetBlackboard` -- engine-declared 3-panel spine
      (Definition / Archetype / Statement); lifecycle: empty until
      `SourceFreeze` is produced, then populated during Target phase.
  end note

  class AbstractionLayer <<engine,record>> {
    +id: String
    +rank: int
    +description: String
  }

  note bottom of AbstractionLayer
    **AbstractionLayer** -- Stratification metadata for panels.

    Convention across both Blackboards: lower `rank` = less integrated
    / more concrete; higher `rank` = more integrated / closer to
    a usable answer. Layers DO NOT enforce data flow -- the panel DAG
    (`Panel.dependsOnPanels`) remains operational truth.

    Source side: each Pack declares its own `abstractionLayers[]` in
    `pack-manifest.json`. Target side: engine ships a fixed 3-layer
    enum (`TargetLayer` below) -- L_DEFINITION (rank 0), L_ARCHETYPE
    (rank 1), L_STATEMENT (rank 2).
  end note

  Blackboard "1" *-- "1..*" Panel : hosts >

  ' ============================================================
  ' PANEL — single Java record (no hierarchy)
  ' ============================================================

  class Panel <<engine,record>> {
    +name: String
    +blackboard: Blackboard
    +abstractionLayer: String
    +slots: Map<String, ContributionSlot>
    +dependsOnPanels: List<String>
  }

  class ContributionSlot <<engine,record>> {
    +name: String
    +panel: Panel
    +schemaUri: URI
    +defaultResolver: ContributionResolver
    +contributions: List<Contribution>
  }

  ' Composition: Panel is a composite of ContributionSlots,
  ' and each ContributionSlot owns its Contributions.
  ' The composition arrows imply the inverse references
  ' (ContributionSlot.panel and Contribution.slot).
  Panel "1" *-- "1..*" ContributionSlot : composes >
  ContributionSlot "1" *-- "0..*" Contribution : holds >

  note bottom of ContributionSlot
    **ContributionSlot** — Composite child of `Panel`; the typed bag
    that owns Contributions of one slot within that Panel.

    **Concept Semantics**:

    - A ContributionSlot is the unit of *typing* AND *resolution* on
      the Blackboard. Every `Contribution` belongs to exactly one
      ContributionSlot (held in `contributions`); every Contribution's
      `post` is validated against this slot's `schemaUri`; every
      conflict among this slot's Contributions is folded by this
      slot's `defaultResolver` (overridable per `(panel, slot)` via
      RunConfig).
    - The slot's *static shape* — `(name, panel, schemaUri,
      defaultResolver)` — is fixed at Pack-registration time and
      sealed for the Run. Its *runtime state* — the `contributions`
      list — grows monotonically as KSs and the Initializer
      post into it. The slot is the only legitimate write target on
      the Blackboard; KSs never reach a Panel directly.
    - The `panel` back-reference makes the slot self-describing
      (a slot without its panel is meaningless: identity-key contract,
      DAG position, and engine-vs-Pack ownership all live on the
      Panel).

    **Field Semantics**:

    - `name`: slot name. Same string as the key under which this slot
      is registered in `panel.slots`. Stable identifier used by
      `Contribution`-wire envelopes (`Contribution.slot` field in
      `panels/Contribution.schema.json`) and by KS descriptors
      (`writesSlots[]`).
    - `panel`: composite parent. Back-reference; the Panel
      determines the hosting Blackboard (`SourceBlackboard` /
      `TargetBlackboard`), DAG
      position, identity-key contract, and engine-vs-Pack ownership.
    - `schemaUri`: versioned `gsmarc://` URI of the JSON Schema bound
      to this slot. Every `Contribution.post` posted into this slot
      MUST satisfy it. Resolved as a JAR resource at
      `/META-INF/gsmarc/<URI-tail>` (no network fetch).
    - `defaultResolver`: the `ContributionResolver` strategy used to
      fold competing Contributions held by this slot. RunConfig may
      override per `(panel, slot)`.
    - `contributions`: live list of `Contribution`s posted into this
      slot during the current Run. Append-only during the Run;
      cleared when the Run ends.

    **Validation Rules (engine-enforced at registration / posting)**:

    - `name` MUST be unique within `panel.slots`.
    - `panel` MUST be the Panel under whose `slots` map this slot is
      registered (composition consistency).
    - `schemaUri` MUST resolve to a bundled JSON Schema (Draft
      2020-12) at registration time.
    - For every `c` in `contributions`: `c.slot == this`; `c.post`
      MUST validate against `schemaUri`; if `panel.blackboard ==
      TargetBlackboard`, the held Contributions MUST be
      `TargetContribution` instances and each MUST carry a present
      `targetIdentityKey`.
  end note

  note bottom of Panel
    **Panel** — Typed region of the Blackboard, modelled as a
    composite of `ContributionSlot`s.

    **Concept Semantics**:

    - A Panel is a *composite container*. Its `slots` map binds each
      slot name to a `ContributionSlot` instance, and each
      `ContributionSlot` in turn owns the live list of
      `Contribution`s posted into it during a Run. The composition
      arrows on the diagram are normative: `Panel →*→ ContributionSlot
      →*→ Contribution`.
    - The `(name, blackboard, abstractionLayer, dependsOnPanels)`
      tuple plus the slot-map shape (slot names + each slot's
      `schemaUri` and `defaultResolver`) is the panel's static
      **registration** metadata. The `contributions` list inside each
      slot is the panel's **runtime** state, populated as a Run
      progresses.
    - Both engine-owned (Target) and Pack-owned (Source) panels are
      instances of THIS record. The engine ships no panel base class
      and no per-panel subclass. Differentiation is by which
      Blackboard instance hosts the panel (the `blackboard`
      back-reference); ownership (engine vs Pack) is derived from
      that instance.
    - The slot map is CLOSED at Pack-registration time. One slot =
      one entry in `slots`; one Contribution belongs to exactly one
      `(panel, slot)` pair and is held in that slot's
      `contributions` list.
    - The Panel knows its place in the engine-validated panel DAG
      via `dependsOnPanels`. The DAG is validated for acyclicity and
      cross-DAG-read containment at Pack registration.

    **Field Semantics**:

    - `name`: panel name. MUST be Pack-namespaced when
      `blackboard == SourceBlackboard` (e.g. `itip:SourceUnit`);
      Target Blackboard panels use unqualified GSM-spine names
      `Definition`, `Archetype`, `Statement` (the three engine-fixed
      Target panels after Wave 9).
    - `blackboard`: composite parent. Back-reference to the hosting
      Blackboard instance (`SourceBlackboard` or `TargetBlackboard`).
      Determines engine-vs-Pack ownership, identity-key contract
      (Target panels REQUIRE `targetIdentityKey` on every
      Contribution; Source panels MAY omit it), the layer registry
      to validate `abstractionLayer` against (Pack-declared for
      Source, engine-fixed `TargetLayer` enum for Target), and the
      DAG context within which `dependsOnPanels` is resolved.
    - `abstractionLayer`: id of the layer this panel belongs to.
      Source panels: MUST be one of the Pack's declared
      `abstractionLayers[]` ids. Target panels: MUST be one of
      `TargetLayer` (`L_DEFINITION` / `L_ARCHETYPE` / `L_STATEMENT`).
      Informational only -- not enforced as a data-flow constraint.
    - `slots`: closed map binding each accepted slot name to a
      `ContributionSlot` (a composite child of this Panel) carrying:
      - `name`: the slot's name (same as the map key).
      - `schemaUri`: versioned `gsmarc://` URI of the JSON Schema
        that every `Contribution.post` posted into this slot MUST
        satisfy.
      - `defaultResolver`: the `ContributionResolver` strategy used
        to fold competing Contributions held by THIS slot. RunConfig
        may override per `(panel, slot)`.
      - `contributions`: live list of `Contribution`s posted into
        this slot during the current Run.
      Engine-defined entries on engine-owned panels are sealed.
      Packs MAY add Pack-namespaced additive entries via
      `pack-manifest.extendsPanels[]`. Schema URIs resolve to
      resources bundled in the engine or Pack JAR at
      `/META-INF/gsmarc/<URI-tail>`.
    - `dependsOnPanels`: panel-DAG edges within THIS panel's
      Blackboard instance. Cross-Blackboard edges are NOT permitted;
      cross-Blackboard data flow is mediated by the `SourceFreeze`
      bridge (Target KSs read frozen Source state via
      `controlContext.sourceFreeze()`).

    **Validation Rules (engine-enforced at registration)**:

    - `name` MUST be unique within `blackboard.panels`.
    - `blackboard == SourceBlackboard` ⇒ `name` MUST be
      Pack-namespaced AND `abstractionLayer` MUST be one of the
      Pack's declared `abstractionLayers[]` ids.
    - `blackboard == TargetBlackboard` ⇒ panel MUST be one of the
      three engine-reserved Target panels (`Definition`, `Archetype`,
      `Statement`) AND `abstractionLayer` MUST be the corresponding
      `TargetLayer` value (Pack manifests cannot declare new Target
      panels in `panels[]`; only additive slot entries are allowed
      via `extendsPanels[]`).
    - `dependsOnPanels` MUST NOT introduce a cycle in the DAG of
      `blackboard`.
    - A Contribution accepted into this Panel MUST carry a
      `slot` that is a key in `slots`; the
      Contribution's `post` MUST validate against the bound schema.
    - A Contribution produced by a KS whose descriptor declares
      `determinismDefault = NON_DETERMINISTIC` MUST carry `cacheKey`
      (I-4).

    **Derivation Rules**:

    - For ENGINE-owned target panels: instances are engine constants
      (see `Panel ontology` below) instantiated by the Blackboard
      Builder substep.
    - For PACK-owned source panels: instances are constructed from
      `pack-manifest.panels[]` entries by the Blackboard Builder.

    **Decision Invariants — when to introduce a new Panel vs a new
    slot** (engine-validated at Pack registration where
    possible; complement to runtime invariants I-1..I-15 in the GSM
    Sourcing Blackboard skill)

    Provenance tag legend:
      [BB]    inherited directly from the canonical Blackboard pattern
              (data-integration variants such as TRICERO, CRYSALIS, GBB
              -- Hearsay-II is the historical reference but not
              the only one; GSM Sourcer is closer to the
              data-integration variants because Source-side input is
              deterministic, not signal-uncertain)
      [GSM-S] GSM Sourcer engineering choice (NOT canonical); kept
              honest so the design tradeoff stays visible

    - **P-1 [BB] Producer/consumer separation**: a new Panel is
      justified IFF at least one consumer reads this typed region
      while WRITING somewhere else. The consumer MAY be another KS
      OR an engine stage (e.g. the Validation/Registration
      Pipeline reads `Confidence` even though no KS does). If no
      consumer exists distinct from the producer KS(s), the
      candidate region is a slot of an existing panel,
      not a new panel.
    - **P-2 [BB] Distinct DAG node**: a new Panel MUST occupy a
      distinct node in the panel DAG. If the candidate would have
      the same `dependsOnPanels` set AND the same downstream
      readers as an existing panel, it is a slot of
      that panel.
    - **P-3 [GSM-S] Resolver granularity (DISSOLVED 2026-04)**:
      previously, GSM Sourcer attached the resolver at panel
      granularity, which forced any aspect needing a different
      resolution strategy to become its own panel — a structural
      tension with P-2 (same-DAG-position aspects must share the
      panel). The resolver is now attached PER
      `(panel, slot)` via
      `slots[ct].defaultResolver`, with RunConfig
      override key `resolvers."<Panel>.<Slot>"`. P-3 no
      longer constrains panel-vs-type decisions. Retained as a
      named ID for traceability; effectively a no-op rule.
    - **P-5 [BB] Independent fillability**: slots of
      the same panel MUST be fillable by independent KSs in any
      order. If two aspects MUST be co-asserted by the same KS in
      one Contribution (a transactional invariant), they are the
      same slot, not two.

    Negative form (anti-patterns the registration validator does NOT
    catch but reviewers MUST):

    - **Type-as-panel** (P-1/P-2 violation): splitting one logical
      level into N panels with identical DAG positions, fragmenting
      the resolved view and forcing readers to do N-way joins.
    - **Panel-as-type** (P-1 violation): folding a distinct
      abstraction level into a slot of an existing
      panel, hiding it from the DAG and denying its readers the
      ability to subscribe independently. (Pre-2026-04 this was
      also a P-3 violation; with P-3 dissolved, only P-1 still
      catches it.)
  end note

  enum TargetLayer {
    L_DEFINITION
    L_ARCHETYPE
    L_STATEMENT
  }

  enum ContributionResolver {
    highestConfidence
    firstWriter
    failOnConflict
    collectAll
    compose
  }

  enum DefinitionSubjectKind {
    STRUCTURE
    MECHANISM
    EFFECTOR
    RECEPTOR
    INTERACTION
    ARCHETYPE
    DIRECTIVE
    NORM
  }

  enum DefinitionVerdict {
    keep
    drop
    splitInto
    mergeWith
  }

  ' ============================================================
  ' TARGET BLACKBOARD ONTOLOGY — engine-owned 3-layer spine
  ' ============================================================

  package "TargetBlackboard ontology — engine-owned 3-layer spine\n(instances of Panel; hosted on TargetBlackboard)" as TGT {

    object "Definition : Panel" as DefinitionPanel {
      name = "Definition"
      blackboard = TargetBlackboard
      abstractionLayer = L_DEFINITION
      slots[Claim].schemaUri = gsmarc://gsm-sourcer/panels/Definition/Claim/v1
      slots[Claim].defaultResolver = highestConfidence
      slots[Merge].schemaUri = gsmarc://gsm-sourcer/panels/Definition/Merge/v1
      slots[Merge].defaultResolver = collectAll
      slots[Verdict].schemaUri = gsmarc://gsm-sourcer/panels/Definition/Verdict/v1
      slots[Verdict].defaultResolver = highestConfidence
      dependsOnPanels = []
    }

    note bottom of DefinitionPanel
      **Definition** — Identity-binding panel of the GSM spine
      (TargetLayer L_DEFINITION).

      **Concept Semantics**:

      - Decides WHICH source items collectively define ONE GSM
        subject (Structure, Mechanism, Effector, Receptor,
        Interaction, Archetype, Directive, Norm). Join key for every
        downstream target panel.
      - Three slots (closed):
        - `Claim` — an `IdentificationKS` asserts an identity for a
          subject based on SourceFreeze evidence. `post` carries
          `subjectKind` (DefinitionSubjectKind), `identityKey`
          (mints the join key), and `supportingSourceIds`.
        - `Merge` — a `ReconciliationKS` asserts that two prior
          identities describe the same subject. `post` carries
          `supersedesIdentityKeys` (non-empty) and a surviving
          `targetIdentityKey`. Identity-time merging (pre-Statement),
          based on Source signals only.
        - `Verdict` — a `GranularityKS` (TOP_DOWN: reads Statement,
          writes here) posts one consolidation verdict per identity.
          `post.verdict` is one of `keep`, `drop`, `splitInto`,
          `mergeWith` (see `DefinitionVerdict` enum). `mergeWith`
          carries `targetIdentityKeys[0]` as the survivor;
          `splitInto` carries the new identities to spawn.
      - Default resolvers (per slot): `Claim` ->
        `highestConfidence`, `Merge` -> `collectAll`, `Verdict` ->
        `highestConfidence`. Equally-confident `Claim`s on the same
        surface key remain side-by-side in `slot.contributions`
        (resolver picks the highest; ties are broken deterministically
        by `(timestamp, id)`).

      **Validation Rules**:

      - `Claim.post.identityKey` is the engine's join key for
        downstream panels; required.
      - `Merge.post.supersedesIdentityKeys[]` MUST resolve to prior
        `Claim` Contributions on the Blackboard.
      - `Verdict.mergeWith` => `targetIdentityKeys` MUST resolve to a
        Definition on the Blackboard. `Verdict.splitInto` =>
        `targetIdentityKeys[]` non-empty; each new identity yields a
        fresh Definition + downstream-target re-fire.

      **Merge precedence rule (Definition.Merge vs Definition.Verdict.mergeWith)**:

      - `Definition.Merge` is identity-time merging (pre-Statement),
        based on Source signals only.
      - `Definition.Verdict.mergeWith` is post-statement consolidation,
        informed by the populated Statement (the GranularityKS reads
        Statement to decide).
      - When both apply to the same identity, `Verdict.mergeWith`
        wins (more informed). The Pipeline's Validation stage uses
        the resolved Verdict for the registered Ascription;
        downstream KSs that re-trigger on a Verdict change recompute
        against the surviving identity.
    end note

    object "Archetype : Panel" as ArchetypePanel {
      name = "Archetype"
      blackboard = TargetBlackboard
      abstractionLayer = L_ARCHETYPE
      slots[Application].schemaUri = gsmarc://gsm-sourcer/panels/Archetype/Application/v1
      slots[Application].defaultResolver = collectAll
      dependsOnPanels = [Definition]
    }

    note bottom of ArchetypePanel
      **Archetype** — Archetype-application panel of the GSM spine
      (TargetLayer L_ARCHETYPE).

      **Concept Semantics**:

      - Captures which GSM Archetype(s) apply to a given Definition.
        One slot (closed):
        - `Application` — an `ArchetypeKS` posts one archetype
          reference per Contribution. `post` carries `archetypeRef`
          (versioned `gsmarc://` URI of the GSM Archetype Definition).
      - Default resolver (`Application`): `collectAll` (union over
        Applications). The Pipeline reads the union as the resolved
        archetype set for the Definition.

      **Validation Rules**:

      - `Application.post.archetypeRef` MUST resolve to a registered
        Archetype.
      - The asserted Archetype's structural-base (allOf chain) MUST
        be compatible with the resolved
        `Definition.Claim.subjectKind` for the same identity.
    end note

    object "Statement : Panel" as StatementPanel {
      name = "Statement"
      blackboard = TargetBlackboard
      abstractionLayer = L_STATEMENT
      slots[Draft].schemaUri = gsmarc://gsm-sourcer/panels/Statement/Draft/v1
      slots[Draft].defaultResolver = compose
      dependsOnPanels = [Archetype]
    }

    note bottom of StatementPanel
      **Statement** — Statement-shaping panel of the GSM spine
      (TargetLayer L_STATEMENT, the most integrated layer).

      **Concept Semantics**:

      - Holds populated GSM statement payloads conforming to the
        resolved Archetype's JSON Schema. One slot (closed):
        - `Draft` — a `StatementShapingKS` posts a partial or full
          statement payload. `post` carries `statement` (the
          archetype-typed payload), `completeness` (`partial` |
          `full`), and `shapingMethod` (free-form classifier such as
          `structural-extraction`, `llm-completion`,
          `confidence-synthesis`).
      - Default resolver (`Draft`): `compose`. Multiple
        StatementShapingKSs may post Contributions populating disjoint
        archetype fields; the engine's schema-driven per-key merge
        assembles the union into the resolved Statement. This is the
        panel-level realisation of cooperative shaping.
      - Wave 9 collapse: a `ConfidenceSynthesisKS` is just another
        StatementShapingKS variant that reads
        `contributionsOf(Statement, identity)` (and their attached
        `Contribution.evidence` arrays), computes a synthesised
        confidence, and posts a refined Statement Contribution whose
        `confidence` value carries the synthesis result. The `compose`
        resolver folds it into the resolved view.

      **Validation Rules**:

      - `Draft.post.statement` MUST validate against the resolved
        Archetype schema for the targeted Definition (incremental
        schema check at post time).
      - LLM-driven KSs (those with `determinismDefault =
        NON_DETERMINISTIC` in their descriptor) produce
        Contributions that MUST carry a `cacheKey` (I-4).
      - The Pipeline's Validation stage rejects compositions that
        remain `partial` after resolution.
    end note
  }

  ' ============================================================
  ' SOURCE BLACKBOARD ONTOLOGY — Pack-owned (placeholder)
  ' ============================================================

  package "SourceBlackboard ontology — Pack-owned, layered\n(instances of Panel; hosted on SourceBlackboard;\nstratified by Pack-declared abstractionLayers)" as SRC {

    note as SrcPlaceholder
      **Source-side panel instances live in Pack manifests.**

      The engine ships zero Source panels. Each Sourcing Pack declares
      its Source panels as `Panel` instances in
      `pack-manifest.panels[]`, with `blackboard = SourceBlackboard`
      and a Pack-namespaced `name`. Each Pack also declares its own
      `abstractionLayers[]` (`{id, rank, description}` records); each
      Source panel cites one of those layer ids in its
      `abstractionLayer` field. Layers are informational stratification
      metadata (visualization, reasoning); the panel DAG remains
      operational truth.

      For the Repository Sourcing Pack, see:
      `itip/def/repository-sourcing-pack/repository-sourcing-pack.puml`

      Currently declared:
      - `itip:SourceInventory`
      - `itip:SourceUnit`
      - `itip:SourceRelation`
      - `itip:SourceInterface`

      Their bridging into the Target Blackboard is no longer a panel
      DAG edge (Wave 9): cross-Blackboard reads are mediated by the
      `SourceFreeze` artefact produced at Source-phase quiescence.
      Target-phase `IdentificationKS` reads SourceFreeze via
      `controlContext.sourceFreeze()` to mint Definition.Claim
      Contributions.
    end note
  }

  ' ============================================================
  ' SOURCE FREEZE (sequential bridge artefact)
  ' ============================================================

  class SourceFreeze <<engine,artifact,immutable>> {
    +freezeId: String
    +runId: String
    +frozenAt: Instant
    +sourcePackUris: List<URI>
    +abstractionLayers: List<AbstractionLayer>
    +panels: Map<String, FrozenPanel>
  }

  note bottom of SourceFreeze
    **SourceFreeze** -- Immutable snapshot of `SourceBlackboard` at
    Source-phase quiescence; the **sequential bridge** between the
    two Blackboards.

    **Lifecycle**:

    1. SourceController runs Source-phase KSs against
       `SourceBlackboard` until quiescence (or
       `runInvariants.completionPredicate` /
       `runInvariants.maxIterations`).
    2. Engine produces a `SourceFreeze` (deep-immutable: every Panel,
       slot, and Contribution copied by value; the Pack-declared
       `abstractionLayers` snapshotted alongside).
    3. SourceController shuts down. TargetController starts.
    4. Target-phase KSs read frozen Source state via
       `controlContext.sourceFreeze()` (returns a `SourceFreezeView`).
       They CANNOT post back to `SourceBlackboard`.

    Distinct from `SourcingRunContext`: SourcingRunContext carries
    Run input (operator intent, scope, focus, profile,
    granularityPolicy, resolver overrides, runInvariants); the
    SourceFreeze carries the Source phase's *output* (resolved Source
    contributions per panel/slot/identity, with their evidence
    payloads).

    **Validation Rules**:

    - Produced exactly once per Run, after Source quiescence and
      before TargetController activation.
    - Immutable: any attempt to mutate after publication is a
      programming error.
    - `panels` keys are exactly the Pack-declared Source panel names
      that participated in the Run.
  end note

  ' ============================================================
  ' EVIDENCE REF (value object on Contribution.evidence[])
  ' ============================================================

  class EvidenceRef <<engine,value>> {
    +source: String
    +kind: String
    +weight: double
    +note: String
  }

  note bottom of EvidenceRef
    **EvidenceRef** -- Value object attached to a Contribution's
    `evidence: List<EvidenceRef>` array; replaces the Wave 9-dropped
    `Evidence` panel.

    Any KS that wants to attach evidence to a Contribution it posts
    populates this list directly. Downstream KSs reading the
    Contribution (via `BlackboardView.contributionsOf(...)` or via
    `SourceFreezeView`) inspect the `evidence` array. A
    `ConfidenceSynthesisKS` reads attached evidence across
    Statement Contributions for an identity, computes a synthesised
    confidence, and posts a refined Statement Contribution whose
    `confidence` value carries the synthesis result.

    Fields:
    - `source` (optional): provenance identifier (e.g. a Source
      Contribution id, an external source uri, a tool result handle).
    - `kind`: free-form classifier (`test-pass`, `test-fail`,
      `interface-coherence`, `relation-density`, `static-analysis`,
      `llm-rationale`, ...).
    - `weight`: in `[-1, 1]`. Negative values are admissible
      (counter-evidence).
    - `note` (optional): short rationale.
  end note

  Contribution "1" *-- "0..*" EvidenceRef : evidence >


  ' ============================================================
  ' CONTRIBUTION (anchor type)
  ' ============================================================

  abstract class Contribution <<engine,record,abstract>> {
    +id: String
    +slot: ContributionSlot
    +post: JsonObject
    +contributorKsId: URI
    +confidence: double
    +rationale: String
    +evidence: List<EvidenceRef>
    +cacheKey: String
    +derivedFrom: List<String>
    +timestamp: Instant
  }

  class SourceContribution <<engine,record>> extends Contribution {
  }

  class TargetContribution <<engine,record>> extends Contribution {
    +targetIdentityKey: String
  }

  note bottom of Contribution
    **Contribution** — Atomic post on the Blackboard. Held by exactly
    one `ContributionSlot`.

    **Concept Semantics**:

    - The unit of work on the Blackboard. Posted by a Knowledge
      Source or by the Initializer (from the Pack's Instructions
      Provider). The producer is always identified by
      `contributorKsId` (a versioned `gsmarc://` URI); an
      engine-reserved URI names the Initializer.
    - Belongs to exactly ONE `ContributionSlot`. The `slot` field is
      the typed back-reference to its composite parent; the slot in
      turn knows its `panel`, so `(panel, slot)` is fully reachable
      via `slot.panel.name + slot.name`. The JSON wire envelope in
      `panels/Contribution.schema.json` carries `panel` and `slot`
      as strings for serialization.
    - **Immutable + append-only**: a Contribution is NEVER mutated in
      place. To "change" a value, post a new Contribution; the old
      one remains in `slot.contributions` for audit. Multiple KSs
      MAY post into the same `(slot, targetIdentityKey)` — that is
      exactly the competition the slot's resolver is designed to
      fold.
    - **Two concrete subtypes** distinguish source-side and
      target-side semantics: `SourceContribution` (posted into a
      panel hosted on `SourceBlackboard`) and `TargetContribution`
      (posted into a panel hosted on `TargetBlackboard`; carries
      the additional `targetIdentityKey`). All other fields are on
      the abstract `Contribution`.
    - The engine attaches `id`, `contributorKsId`, `derivedFrom`,
      `timestamp`, and `cacheKey`. KSs cannot fabricate them.

    **Property Semantics** (abstract `Contribution`):

    - `id: String` — engine-set unique id. The only stable handle for
      `derivedFrom` graphs and audit. Distinct from `cacheKey`
      because it is minted *after* work completes; `cacheKey` is
      computed *before* work starts so the engine can skip redundant
      LLM calls.
    - `slot: ContributionSlot` — typed back-reference to the
      composite parent. Navigational truth for reaching the schema
      (`slot.schemaUri`), the resolver (`slot.defaultResolver`), the
      panel (`slot.panel`), and the sibling Contributions
      (`slot.contributions`).
    - `post: JsonObject` — the actual payload posted on the
      Blackboard. MUST validate against `slot.schemaUri`. Everything
      else on the record is metadata wrapping it.
    - `contributorKsId: URI` — versioned `gsmarc://` URI of the
      producer (KS or Pack Instructions Provider). Provenance,
      audit, sandbox attribution, and KS-version-pinning input for
      `cacheKey`. Engine-set; KSs cannot forge it. The provenance
      class (KS / Initializer) is read from the URI prefix; no
      separate `kind` field is kept.
    - `confidence: double` — the producer's self-rated credibility
      in this single post, in `[0, 1]`. MANDATORY (deterministic
      structural posts conventionally set `1.0`). Used by the
      `highestConfidence` resolver and by `ConfidenceSynthesisKS`,
      which reads `contributionsOf(Statement, identity)` and posts
      a refined `Statement.Draft` Contribution carrying the
      synthesised cross-KS confidence (Wave 9: the dropped
      `Confidence` panel is no longer needed — confidence rides on
      every Contribution and is synthesised in place).
    - `rationale: String` — optional free-text explanation. Surfaced
      in audit trails. Empty by default.
    - `cacheKey: String` — stable input fingerprint, set by the
      engine when the producing KS is declared
      `determinismDefault = NON_DETERMINISTIC` in its descriptor
      (I-4). Computed as a hash of `(contributorKsId, all read
      inputs)`; lets the engine memoise LLM calls across iterations
      and Run replays. Null when the producing KS is deterministic.
      Determinism is a property of the KS implementation, not of an
      individual Contribution: two KSs writing into the same slot
      may have opposite determinism, so the flag lives on the KS
      descriptor (`KnowledgeSourceDescriptor.determinismDefault`),
      not on the Contribution itself.
    - `derivedFrom: List<String>` — ids of Contributions the
      producer read to produce this one. Engine-set (the engine
      instruments `BlackboardView` reads). Used for audit and
      lineage reconstruction.
    - `timestamp: Instant` — wall-clock posting time. Required by
      the `firstWriter` resolver and by audit ordering. Engine-set.

    **Property Semantics** (`TargetContribution` only):

    - `targetIdentityKey: String` — identity key on the GSM target
      spine. The slot's resolver folds Contributions per identity
      key. Always present on `TargetContribution`; absent (by type)
      on `SourceContribution`.

    **Validation Rules**:

    - `slot` MUST be a registered `ContributionSlot` (i.e.
      `slot == slot.panel.slots.get(slot.name)`).
    - `post` MUST validate against `slot.schemaUri`.
    - `slot.panel.blackboard == TargetBlackboard` ⇒ instance MUST be a
      `TargetContribution` and `targetIdentityKey` MUST be present.
    - `slot.panel.blackboard == SourceBlackboard` ⇒ instance MUST be a
      `SourceContribution`.
    - Producer determinism is read from
      `KnowledgeSourceDescriptor.determinismDefault`;
      `NON_DETERMINISTIC` ⇒ `cacheKey` MUST be present (I-4);
      `DETERMINISTIC` ⇒ `cacheKey` MUST be null.
    - `confidence` MUST be in `[0, 1]`.
  end note

  ' ============================================================
  ' SOURCING RUN CONTEXT (engine run state)
  ' ============================================================

  package "Engine run state\n(distinct from the Blackboard)" as ERS {

    class SourcingRunContext <<engine,record,immutable>> {
      +runId: String
      +profile: JsonObject
      +instructionsPayload: JsonObject
      +scope: Scope
      +focus: Focus
      +runInvariants: RunInvariants
      +resolverOverrides: Map<String, ContributionResolver>
      +externalToolBindings: List<ExternalToolBinding>
    }

    note bottom of SourcingRunContext
      **SourcingRunContext** — Frozen run-scoped engine value (NOT a
      panel).

      **Concept Semantics**:

      - Built by the `Initializer` in five substeps: Plug-in Loader →
        Instructions Provider → Scope Builder → Focus Builder →
        freeze `SourcingRunContext` → Blackboard Builder. The freeze
        happens BEFORE the Blackboard Builder stands up the panels,
        so the Run state is fully determined before any KS can run.
      - Read by all KSs as a read-only value via
        `controlContext.runContext()`. The deliberate departure from
        Hearsay-II: the Run input lives HERE, not as a Blackboard
        hypothesis (I-1).

      **Field Semantics**:

      - `profile`: operator-supplied profile (free-form Pack-typed).
      - `instructionsPayload`: forwarded verbatim from RunConfig to
        the Pack's Instructions Provider.
      - `scope`: derived `{ inclusion[], exclusion[], axisDecision }`.
      - `focus`: derived `{ priorityBands[] }`.
      - `runInvariants`: `{ maxIterations, quiescenceThreshold,
        determinismMode, completionPredicate? }`.
      - `resolverOverrides`: per-panel resolver overrides.
      - `externalToolBindings`: operator-narrowed bindings of the
        Pack's `requestedExternalTools[]` to host paths.

      **Validation Rules**:

      - Frozen after Initialization. Any mutation attempt MUST raise.
      - `runInvariants.completionPredicate`, when set, MUST resolve
        to a loadable Java class implementing the engine's
        `CompletionPredicate` interface.
    end note
  }

  ' ============================================================
  ' RELATIONSHIPS
  ' ============================================================

  ' Panel <-> Contribution
  Panel ..> Contribution : <<accepts>>

  ' Two Blackboard instances of the generic Blackboard class
  Blackboard <|.. SourceBlackboard
  Blackboard <|.. TargetBlackboard
  SourceBlackboard ..> SrcPlaceholder : <<hosts>>
  TargetBlackboard ..> DefinitionPanel : <<hosts>>
  TargetBlackboard ..> ArchetypePanel : <<hosts>>
  TargetBlackboard ..> StatementPanel : <<hosts>>

  ' Target-side DAG (BOTTOM_UP)
  DefinitionPanel --> ArchetypePanel
  ArchetypePanel --> StatementPanel

  ' Target-side TOP_DOWN edge: GranularityKS reads Statement, writes Definition.Verdict
  StatementPanel ..> DefinitionPanel : <<TOP_DOWN\n(Definition.Verdict)>>

  ' Sequential Source -> Target bridge via SourceFreeze
  SourceBlackboard ..> SourceFreeze : <<frozen at\nquiescence>>
  SourceFreeze ..> TargetBlackboard : <<read by\nTarget KSs>>

  ' Engine run state -> Blackboard (built BEFORE panels)
  SourcingRunContext ..> Panel : <<frozen before\nBlackboard Builder>>
}

@enduml
